{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Simeon and Levi, brothers.</b> Because of the deed of Shechem." "<b>Their weapons.</b> Some say from הכרת פניהם (Isaiah 3:9), and it is not correct grammatically. Some say their acquisitions, like \"you shall buy from them\" (Deuteronomy 2:6), but תכרו is only from the root of digging. Some say from the root of selling, that they sold themselves, like \"a people that risks its life to death\" (Judges 5:18). The correct interpretation in my eyes is that it is from the formation of מְכרֹותַיִךְ (Ezekiel 16:3), and it is missing a bet, like what is found in בית ד׳ (2 Kings 16:8), \"which I commanded as a dwelling\" (1 Samuel 2:29). The meaning concerns the violence they committed, that after they brought the men of Shechem into a covenant, they killed them by treachery."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:21.333734702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}